From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:11:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(config): an always approval keeps the managed settings in
 config.yaml

save_permanent_allowlist loaded the merged config and wrote it back through save_config, which strips every leaf the managed layer pins. A deployment whose init renders the managed values into config.yaml (the user layer merged with HERMES_MANAGED_DIR) lost all of them on the first always answer. The save is now a single-key write of command_allowlist, read and written under a new cross-process lock (config.yaml.lock), so two processes answering always at once both land. save_config takes the same lock and keeps each managed leaf as it is on disk instead of deleting it; the caller's value of a managed leaf is still never written.
